 "describes": "Each foot's floor contact is a rigid convex slab whose bottom is a shallow rocker (rise 0.28 mm at the heel end, 0.59 mm at the toe end over a 36 mm contact span, 27 mm wide), its lowest point 1.0 mm below the printed sole (the owner's ~1 mm bicycle inner-tube rubber, 2026-11-23). The profile is built from the robot's measured trunk rotation r(cx) (foot_variant.resolve_crown: contact x_c = cx + h*theta, slope tan(theta), h 135 mm), so the robot rocks on it as the real feet do on the rubber, and it ends where the robot tips (cx 5.8 and 28.6 mm). A FIT of an effective contact to the 2026-11-23 sweeps, not printed geometry: the printed flat is 0.5-1.2 mm longer at the heel and 10-14 mm longer at the toe; the real mechanism (rubber compression, foot or ankle compliance) is not separated.",
